sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 3, docs/reference/task-containers.md): the workspace part of a task start on a task container. It is the workspace part of the task VM path (docs/reference/tasks.md, Provision an external group) without change: the container is a Node with a WireGuard address, an SSH host key and the managed user `orbit`, so every workspace step reaches it as it reaches a task VM.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: task:start
  %% kind: tasks.provision
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane TC icon=server pill=task container tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve · Swamp Node
  participant TC as Task container<br/>HOST-tvm-N
  Note over GW: Capture the workspace<br/>Instance task-GROUP
  %%> What it records:
  %%> - the workspace Instance `task-GROUP` on the container's Node, its start commit, its Route and Process definitions, with the same actions as `instance:create`
  %%> - the guest's SSH targets with `host_keys: null`; the start step's pinned key fills them later
  SW->>GW: Mint the clone token<br/>purpose: clone
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a step mints its token when it runs; admission mints nothing, because a wait for a place can outlast the token
  SW->>SW: Clone on the Swamp Node<br/>full history · bundle
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - clones the Project with full history on the Swamp Node; the credential never reaches the container
  SW->>TC: Copy and import<br/>ssh copy · git fetch
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - copies the bundle over WireGuard and imports it into `<apps>/<project>/workspace`; `origin` stays the plain repository URL
  SW->>TC: Check out the branch<br/>task-GROUP at start commit
  SW->>GW: Mint a read token<br/>purpose: dependencies
  SW->>TC: Run the Project setup<br/>env -C checkout · as orbit
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the Composer and npm configuration with the read token, runs each setup step with its own timeout, output to a file in a private run directory
  SW->>TC: Remove the auth files<br/>and revoke the token
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes both files and revokes the token, on success and on failure; the receipt names `dependency_token`
  SW->>TC: Inspect the source<br/>HEAD · branch · composer.json
  opt the workspace has a Route
    SW->>SW: Route the workspace<br/>operation-route-create
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - holds the Route Nodes, creates the private Route on the development Cluster, releases the hold; Caddy on the router reaches the container's WireGuard address, as it reaches a task VM
  end
  alt the workspace is accepted
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>source_resolved or active
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code · failed_step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the group ends `failed`; the release removes the container with its checkout
  end
